  "note": "Thunderwell Core floor v3b. Masters are the @2x PNGs, drawn at half size. floor_tiles and glow_mask are 1024x64, eight slots of 128x64: a and b plain, c straight, d top/bottom bend, e T with a node, f end node, g cross, h side bend. Untraced cells use a and b only. The slot map and ports_by_flip live in strip. Four pad-to-pad routes stay in routes. glow_mask is lossless data with no source_color: R is emission over the full range, G is 1 along traces with no direction, B is 0. Glow is R * glow_strength * pulse(G) * highlight_dim, tint #47F280. glow_strength is 0.38, inside 0.35 to 0.42. A Thunderwell move tile uses a brighter cyan fill and rim so it stays at least 1.5 times a full-pulse trace. The pulse phase is the cell index over the route length; a shared cell keeps the lower index; flips do not move it. A highlight multiplies the trace by 0.4. The pillar is the painted beam, additive at 0.45, light pool anchored on the cell. room_edge_dark is the green-slate vignette. Pads keep their names and sizes. 2D HDR and bloom stay on the preview.",
